N:pmtiles
D:Use when creating, inspecting, extracting, serving, or troubleshooting PMTiles single-file map tile archives on cloud storage or local disk. Covers PMTiles v3 specification, header inspection (min/max zoom, bounds, clustered directories), converting MBTiles or directories with the pmtiles CLI or go-pmtiles, configuring HTTP Range Requests on S3, R2, GCS, or GitHub Pages, client integration with MapLibre GL JS, Leaflet, OpenLayers, and Python readers. Route format-only skill linting to skill-standardization, raw cloud deployment to deployment-automation, and custom vector graphic shaders to paper-shaders.
G:pmtiles protomaps geospatial map-tiles cloud-storage vector-tiles raster-tiles s3 r2 mvt maplibre
U[5]:
  Inspect PMTiles v3 binary header, zoom bounds, and tile compression offline
  Convert MBTiles archives into optimized single-file PMTiles v3 datasets
  Configure S3, Cloudflare R2, or GCS CORS and HTTP Range request headers
  Extract geographic bounding boxes and zoom subsets from global planet archives
  Integrate PMTiles vector and raster sources into MapLibre GL JS and Leaflet
S[6]{n,action,details}:
  1,Preflight,Run scripts/preflight.py --json to verify CLI tooling and validate archive headers
  2,Convert,Convert SQLite MBTiles or directory tiles to PMTiles v3 using pmtiles convert
  3,Inspect,Examine header fields and JSON metadata via pmtiles show or scripts/preflight.py
  4,Extract,Subset regional bounds using pmtiles extract with --bbox and --maxzoom flags
  5,Storage,Configure object storage bucket CORS to expose Content-Range and allow Range headers
  6,Client,Register pmtiles.Protocol with MapLibre GL JS or Leaflet and add pmtiles:// sources
R[5]:
  Run scripts/preflight.py --archive <path> before deploying or serving local PMTiles archives
  Ensure cloud storage exposes Content-Range and ETag headers; otherwise range queries fail
  Use pmtiles extract to subset planet files rather than re-rendering tiles from raw vectors
  Verify tile_type matches client expectations (MVT vector vs PNG/JPEG/WEBP raster)
  Route format linting to skill-standardization and raw cloud infrastructure to deployment-automation
